s, planes and geometric relationships in space.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 27, Unit 3 Topic 3"},{"title":"3.4 Vector calculus","detail":"Differentiate and integrate vector functions and analyse position, velocity and acceleration.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 28, Unit 3 Topic 4"},{"title":"3.5 Further matrices","detail":"Use matrix inverses, determinants, eigenvalues and transformations in extended applications.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 29, Unit 3 Topic 5"},{"title":"4.1 Integration techniques","detail":"Apply substitution, integration by parts and partial fractions to evaluate integrals.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 31, Unit 4 Topic 1"},{"title":"4.2 Applications of integral calculus","detail":"Use integrals for areas, volumes and other mathematical and practical applications.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 32, Unit 4 Topic 2"},{"title":"4.3 Rates of change and differential equations","detail":"Form, solve and interpret first-order differential equations and rate models.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 33, Unit 4 Topic 3"},{"title":"4.4 Modelling motion","detail":"Model motion using vector calculus, differential equations and force relationships.","startsOn":null,"endsOn":null,"startTerm":null,"startWeek":null,"endTerm":null,"endWeek":null,"sourceReference":"Printed page 33, Unit 4 Topic 4"},{"title":"4.5 Statistical inference","detail":"Use sample means, confidence intervals and the cen